# Data Safety (Autonomous Mode)

## Never delete or overwrite

- User personal files outside this repo (especially `d:\Jingxuan's Resumes\`, Desktop, Documents, Downloads)
- `.env`, credentials, API keys, tokens, browser profiles with login state
- Git history via `push --force`, `git clean -fdx` on unknown paths, or wiping unrelated drives
- Production databases or anything outside `d:\resume-agent`
- The master resume templates in `d:\Jingxuan's Resumes\` (read-only reference; copy into repo if needed)

## Allowed cleanup (project-local only)

- `archive/artifacts/` old screenshots/reports when regenerating the same iter
- `__pycache__/`, `.next/`, `node_modules/.cache/`, pytest caches inside the repo
- Generated files under `data/` that the app itself creates (drafts, artifacts), except do not wipe all of `data/` blindly
- Temp scripts you created in the repo (e.g. `_tmp_*.py`)

## Destructive git

- `git reset --hard` only to a known `checkpoint/iter-*-pass` tag **in this repo** after a failed iteration
- Never delete remote branches or force-push to `main`

## Apply boundary

- Fill ATS forms only via ghost-driver-mcp + `.agents/skills/jobright-apply` in Agent chat
- **Must stop before Submit**; never click Submit / Submit Application
